# Compiler edge cases that compile and run: errors in param defaults show
# the fn they belong to (a self tail call's rerun default too), an extern
# returning `const char *`, raw high bytes in a string literal, 190
# nested parentheses and a 900-link operator chain, and a long string
# literal.

extern include "netdb.h"
extern fn hstrerror(err: Int) -> String

fn show_stack(r)
  print(r.ok, r.error)
  for f in r.stack
    print("  at", f.name, f.line)
  end
end

fn needs_len(s, n = len(s))
  n
end
show_stack(pcall(fn() needs_len(5) end))

fn label(n)
  if n == 1
    error("no label for 1")
  end
  "n{n}"
end
fn countdown(n, tag = label(n))
  if n == 0
    return "done"
  end
  countdown(n - 1)
end
show_stack(pcall(fn() countdown(3) end))
print(countdown(0))

print(hstrerror(1) != "")

let raw = "ÿþx"
print(len(raw), ord(raw, 0), ord(raw, 2))

